====== FriendlyARM NanoPi R4S ======

The NanoPi R4S is made by FriendlyElec for IoT applications. It includes the RK3399 SoC, two 1Gbps Ethernet ports, microSD storage, and 4GB LPDDR4 RAM. The NanoPi R4S Enterprise Edition adds an additional EEPROM for the MAC address. These models are supported by official builds of OpenWrt.

The R4S model with 1GB RAM and the R4SE with onboard 32GB eMMC are not officially supported however have custom builds available.

{{:media:friendlyarm:r4s_01-900x630.jpg?450|FriendlyARM NanoPi R4S}}

**support forum:** https://forum.openwrt.org/t/nanopi-r4s-rk3399-is-a-great-new-openwrt-device/79143/1741
